rol Project"},{"type":"h","text":"1 Research Internship / Laboratory Project"}]},{"heading":"Best Overall Positioning","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"flow","items":["Quantum Science & Engineering","Quantum Physics + Electronics","Quantum Device/Control Engineering","Quantum Hardware R&D"]},{"type":"p","text":"The strongest graduate profile is not simply “Quantum Computing Student.”"},{"type":"p","text":"A differentiated profile is:"},{"type":"p","text":"“Quantum Hardware Engineer with strong quantum mechanics, electronics, device physics, Python-based scientific computing, experimental measurement, quantum control and hardware-characterization skills.”"},{"type":"p","text":"For this career, the most important long-term combination is:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Quantum Physics","Hardware Engineering","Experimental Skills","Scientific Computing","Research"],"sep":"+"},{"type":"flow","items":["This creates a pathway from Junior Quantum Hardware Engineer / Research Engineer","Quantum Hardware Engineer","Senior Device/Control Engineer","Principal Quantum Engineer","Quantum Systems Architect or Quantum Hardware R&D Leader"]}]}]}